    {
      "id": "volume_price_dissonance",
      "name": "Volume-Price Dissonance",
      "class_name": "",
      "description": "This signal identifies instances where the price movement is inconsistent with volume trends, measuring the divergence between price changes and volume changes over a recent window.",
      "formula": "",
      "trading_idea": "The hypothesis is that a significant divergence between price movement and volume can indicate a potential reversal or continuation of the trend. When price increases with low volume or decreases with high volume, it suggests a lack of conviction in the price move, making it likely to reverse. This mechanism persists against arbitrage because it captures behavioral biases of market participants who may overreact to price changes while underestimating the role of volume in validating those moves.",
